1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,181
Submit a coherent portfolio rather
than disconnected templates.

2
00:00:04,251 --> 00:00:09,265
The Site Map should support the Frame Card, the
prediction should match its outcome, the build

3
00:00:09,335 --> 00:00:14,391
should test the critical uncertainty, and the
delta log should compare against the prediction.

4
00:00:14,461 --> 00:00:19,815
Include the landing checklist, ownership plan,
second reading, distill pack, and one-page

5
00:00:19,885 --> 00:00:24,664
decision memo. Score seven
dimensions using observable criteria.

6
00:00:24,734 --> 00:00:31,091
A high aggregate score cannot compensate for
an unauthorized action or fabricated evidence.

7
00:00:31,161 --> 00:00:34,937
One submission has beautiful
slides but no written prediction.

8
00:00:35,007 --> 00:00:39,765
Another has a modest prototype and clear
evidence connecting every decision.

9
00:00:39,835 --> 00:00:45,552
Presentation quality supports readability, while
the rubric evaluates delivery reasoning and

10
00:00:45,622 --> 00:00:46,646
behavior.

11
00:00:46,716 --> 00:00:51,495
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

12
00:00:51,565 --> 00:00:57,069
Score your portfolio using the rubric, then
check every safety and evidence gate separately.

13
00:00:57,139 --> 00:01:03,432
Use zero for absent evidence, one for description,
two for partial demonstration, three for a

14
00:01:03,502 --> 00:01:09,262
coherent supported result, and four for strong
demonstration with limitations and transfer.

15
00:01:09,332 --> 00:01:13,812
The proposed pass threshold is seventy
percent plus all mandatory gates.

16
00:01:13,882 --> 00:01:18,831
This is an educational scoring design,
not an accredited competency standard.

17
00:01:18,901 --> 00:01:21,461
Can a high score offset invented evidence?

18
00:01:21,531 --> 00:01:25,094
A. No, evidence integrity is a mandatory gate B.

19
00:01:25,164 --> 00:01:27,297
Yes, if the prototype works C.

20
00:01:27,367 --> 00:01:29,415
Yes, if the slides are polished.

21
00:01:29,485 --> 00:01:30,936
The best answer is A.

22
00:01:31,006 --> 00:01:34,462
Mandatory gates remain separate
from the aggregate score.
